<header class="page-hero">
  <h1>skyBlip Go, subject by subject.</h1>
  <p class="page-hero-subtitle">
    Seven guides, with the screens as the firmware draws them.
  </p>
</header>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">In flight</h2>
  <div class="guide-cards">
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "far-all.png", alt: "The radar page in PLOT ALL, traffic inside the ring and on the band around it" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "radar" %></h3>
      <p>The radar keeps your direction of travel at the top and shows each aircraft's predicted path for the next minute. An alarm tells you where to look, and a list shows nearby aircraft.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "sixpack.png", alt: "The six-dial page" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "instruments" %></h3>
      <p>Six dials show GPS and barometer readings, for fun. The battery level sits above the middle dial. On the Go+, a g-meter records the flight's peak loads.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "astern-all.png", alt: "The radar page in PLOT ALL with a group of aircraft behind you" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "displays" %></h3>
      <p>See every page, every menu and every on-screen request, with the radar in both display modes.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">On the ground</h2>
  <div class="guide-cards">
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-radar.png", alt: "The settings menu" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "controls" %></h3>
      <p>Two controls, a pad and a button, let you change settings in the radar menu, enter your callsign on the device, and open diagnostic pages.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "off-flat-battery.png", alt: "The screen of a device that has switched off because its battery is empty" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "power" %></h3>
      <p>See what it waits for on the apron, what it looks like when off, and how the battery warns as it drains.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "confirm.png", alt: "The authorisation prompt on the screen" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "phone" %></h3>
      <p>Three apps with no pairing, every change asked on the screen, and firmware from the browser.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">For the curious</h2>
  <div class="resource-cards">
    <article>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "radio" %></h3>
      <p>One radio uses four time slots a second and receives signals from two systems in the same slot.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "see-and-avoid" %></h3>
      <p>The published figures for see and avoid cover field of view, the sector scanned, an aircraft's apparent size and reaction time.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "roadmap" %></h3>
      <p>Read about <%= link_to_page "skyblip-bravo", label: "skyBlip Bravo" %> and <%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "Tango" %> for ADS-B on board, the skyBlip Panel for glass cockpits, and the skyPost ground stations.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
